cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IBR-FaultScreen, please cite it as below."
title: "IBR-FaultScreen: fault-scenario screening for grids with inverter-based resources"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ibrahim
    given-names: Shaibu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-5942-9702"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ishaibu/ibr-faultscreen"
keywords:
  - power systems
  - inverter-based resources
  - transient stability
  - fault screening
  - ride-through
  - PRC-029
  - interconnection studies
abstract: >-
  IBR-FaultScreen simulates three-phase fault scenarios on power systems with
  inverter-based resources (solar, wind, battery storage) using ANDES, labels each
  scenario by failure mode (rotor-angle instability, slow voltage recovery, NERC
  PRC-029-1 ride-through exposure, frequency), and trains a screening classifier
  that ranks new scenarios for detailed study, verifying every risky result by
  simulation. It is a screening aid and does not replace an interconnection study.
